WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:20.676
Resync By Bajingan, Toa Pek Yuna

2
00:02:24.787 --> 00:02:31.420
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna. Krishna;
Krishna; Hare; Hare.''

3
00:02:31.852 --> 00:02:38.985
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna. Krishna;
Krishna; Hare; Hare.''

4
00:02:39.217 --> 00:02:42.846
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna.''

5
00:02:43.451 --> 00:02:46.978
''You dwell in my heart.''

6
00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:50.383
''Whether its dusk or dawn.''

7
00:02:50.783 --> 00:02:53.377
''Whether in light or darkness.''

8
00:02:53.449 --> 00:02:56.782
''You're always with me.''

9
00:02:57.049 --> 00:03:00.143
lt was my mother's dying wish..

10
00:03:00.782 --> 00:03:04.309
..to take the entire 'Bhajan
Mandli' group along with their family..

11
00:03:05.048 --> 00:03:06.811
..on a trip to Badrinath.

12
00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:10.007
Please do come.

13
00:03:11.047 --> 00:03:12.241
Of course.

14
00:03:12.313 --> 00:03:14.042
Please join us on the trip..

15
00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.408
..and pray for my mother's soul.

16
00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:22.269
My mother.

17
00:03:25.744 --> 00:03:29.305
Why do souls become
restless after they die?

18
00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.836
l mean, once you're dead
it's the end of all problems.

19
00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.002
Why become restless?

20
00:03:34.076 --> 00:03:35.407
That's not it.

21
00:03:37.276 --> 00:03:41.007
Suppose the deceased
has a unfulfilled wish.

22
00:03:41.108 --> 00:03:43.133
Then his son will fulfil it.

23
00:03:43.775 --> 00:03:45.265
You won't go on the trip.

24
00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:48.834
Get that.

25
00:03:48.907 --> 00:03:51.171
Her mother was in the hospital
for two years.

26
00:03:51.308 --> 00:03:52.775
And he didn't even come take a look.

27
00:03:53.407 --> 00:03:55.272
He was making dollars in America.

28
00:03:55.873 --> 00:03:58.398
This charade is for the world.

29
00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.931
Not for his mother's soul.

30
00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:03.873
No need to look so depressed..

31
00:04:03.939 --> 00:04:05.236
..you won't get an off.

32
00:04:05.306 --> 00:04:07.934
Get that.

33
00:04:15.003 --> 00:04:17.767
Just one idol left!

34
00:04:18.304 --> 00:04:20.135
By the way, where's the trip headed?

35
00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.035
l can't believe you're coming with us.

36
00:04:31.101 --> 00:04:33.001
The children are so happy.

37
00:04:35.067 --> 00:04:36.034
She thinks you are crazy.

38
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.362
l am going on a visit to the temple.
- ''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna.''

39
00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.994
''Krishna; Krishna; Hare; Hare.''

40
00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:44.658
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna.''

41
00:04:44.732 --> 00:04:48.031
''Krishna; Krishna; Hare; Hare.''

42
00:04:54.731 --> 00:04:55.823
Where is he?

43
00:05:01.864 --> 00:05:04.094
- A dozen of
pot-bellied Ganesh idols. - What!

44
00:05:04.629 --> 00:05:06.597
Those Krishnas worth 250.

45
00:05:07.063 --> 00:05:08.963
Eight of those brawny Hanumans.

46
00:05:09.895 --> 00:05:11.988
- What are you saying? - And
five of those 'Sherawali'.

47
00:05:12.029 --> 00:05:13.223
The lady sitting on the tiger.

48
00:05:14.728 --> 00:05:15.717
What's the total?

49
00:05:15.795 --> 00:05:17.558
Three dozen, sir.
- Three dozen, right!

50
00:05:17.994 --> 00:05:20.189
Then, three Sai Babas bonus.
- What?

51
00:05:20.594 --> 00:05:22.061
They are in a big demand.

52
00:05:22.794 --> 00:05:25.126
Send it to the white
Volvo parked there. - Okay.

53
00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.718
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna.''

54
00:05:50.956 --> 00:05:52.583
What did you give him?

55
00:05:53.223 --> 00:05:56.715
Give me too. - Funny, people are
distributing alcohol like offerings..

56
00:06:03.887 --> 00:06:05.115
What's that?

57
00:06:06.553 --> 00:06:07.611
What should l say?

58
00:06:07.754 --> 00:06:09.016
Water of Ganges.
- Yes, yes.

59
00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.585
Oh, give me some.

60
00:06:15.586 --> 00:06:16.746
Why is it so bitter?

61
00:06:16.952 --> 00:06:18.510
Because the Ganges is polluted.

62
00:06:18.752 --> 00:06:20.014
Oh!
- Yes.

63
00:06:25.717 --> 00:06:28.845
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna.''

64
00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:32.645
''Krishna; Krishna; Hare; Hare.''

65
00:06:32.716 --> 00:06:36.015
''Hare Rama; Hare Krishna.''

66
00:06:36.116 --> 00:06:39.745
''Krishna; Krishna; Hare; Hare.''

67
00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:43.814
Apologise. They were fasting.

68
00:06:46.781 --> 00:06:48.874
Hello.
- We were fasting.

69
00:06:48.948 --> 00:06:50.506
And you gave us alcohol.

70
00:06:50.681 --> 00:06:52.512
Alcohol is permitted in fasts.

71
00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.673
lt's made from sugarcane.

72
00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:59.974
lt fills you with energy,
and makes you lightheaded.

73
00:07:00.979 --> 00:07:03.447
- Rascal. Keep the phone down.
- You'll never learn.

74
00:07:03.545 --> 00:07:05.877
Abusing in the month of
'Shravan' (pious month).

75
00:07:06.045 --> 00:07:09.913
See. Truth sounds bitter than liquor.

76
00:07:09.977 --> 00:07:11.410
There's a limit to cracking jokes.

77
00:07:11.478 --> 00:07:12.638
Papa, please.

78
00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.770
What you did yesterday,
is a sin in mummy's view.

79
00:07:15.844 --> 00:07:18.779
And mummy's fasting
today to repent for it.

80
00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:20.737
l want to know.

81
00:07:21.076 --> 00:07:23.874
How can she repent
for my sins by fasting?

82
00:07:24.875 --> 00:07:28.470
Sushila, it's like
your phone's on charging..

83
00:07:28.575 --> 00:07:29.940
..and my battery's getting charged.

84
00:07:30.575 --> 00:07:31.633
ls it Wi-fi?

85
00:07:33.008 --> 00:07:34.839
Chintu, careful.

86
00:07:34.908 --> 00:07:35.966
Papa.

87
00:07:36.841 --> 00:07:37.830
Get down.

88
00:07:37.907 --> 00:07:39.932
Papa, we're practising.

89
00:07:40.073 --> 00:07:41.700
Today's 'Janmastami'.

90
00:07:41.773 --> 00:07:43.138
You've your exams tomorrow.

91
00:07:43.406 --> 00:07:44.839
Who will write that?

92
00:07:45.506 --> 00:07:46.530
Get down!

93
00:07:46.605 --> 00:07:48.095
Why do you always stop
for religious things?

94
00:07:49.039 --> 00:07:50.131
He'll be absolutely fine.

95
00:07:50.805 --> 00:07:52.397
My son's playing Govinda.

96
00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:55.566
My son won't become
Govinda or Chunkey Pandey.

97
00:07:57.037 --> 00:07:58.436
He'll grow up to become a cricketer.

98
00:07:58.504 --> 00:07:59.732
Get down. Get down.

99
00:07:59.904 --> 00:08:00.893
Come on.

100
00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:07.869
Mahadev.
- Coming.

101
00:08:07.969 --> 00:08:09.960
- Let's go.
- Come soon.

102
00:08:10.035 --> 00:08:12.469
Listen.
Remove the tag of Rs.250 from..

103
00:08:12.502 --> 00:08:15.630
..all the new idols that we bought.
- Yes.

104
00:08:16.735 --> 00:08:20.432
Now, watch how l sell
it for 10-12 thousand.

105
00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:23.561
And keep one idol from
each on display. - Okay.

106
00:08:23.966 --> 00:08:25.024
Understand?
- Yes.

107
00:08:26.333 --> 00:08:27.391
Come on.

108
00:08:29.966 --> 00:08:32.560
One and only one piece in the world.

109
00:08:33.899 --> 00:08:36.026
This idol appeared from the ground..
- Yes.

110
00:08:36.465 --> 00:08:38.956
..when the temple at
Badrinath was being built.

111
00:08:39.365 --> 00:08:40.696
What are you saying?

112
00:08:40.831 --> 00:08:44.528
A great sage from Dwarka set
out for a journey on foot..

113
00:08:44.997 --> 00:08:47.625
..and that afternoon the
sun was really scorching..

114
00:08:47.696 --> 00:08:49.357
..l gave him a jug of water to drink.

115
00:08:49.796 --> 00:08:52.993
He was so pleased.

116
00:08:53.529 --> 00:08:55.656
And gave me this idol.

117
00:08:56.029 --> 00:08:58.827
And this idol turned my luck around.

118
00:08:59.362 --> 00:09:00.852
l bought this, once a rented shop..

119
00:09:00.995 --> 00:09:03.896
..and a three room
house in Bhooleshwar.

120
00:09:04.728 --> 00:09:05.854
With terrace.

121
00:09:05.927 --> 00:09:07.451
With terrace.

122
00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.686
Amazing!

123
00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.627
Mr. Kanji, sell this idol to me.

124
00:09:13.426 --> 00:09:15.326
l am in big trouble.

125
00:09:15.826 --> 00:09:19.421
l'll rot in hell
if l even think of selling my Lord.

126
00:09:19.492 --> 00:09:21.756
Sell the God? Look
at what he's saying.

127
00:09:22.358 --> 00:09:23.791
Mischievous... Lord.

128
00:09:25.591 --> 00:09:26.819
Listen carefully.
- Yes.

129
00:09:26.891 --> 00:09:28.518
You can hear His flute.

130
00:09:28.924 --> 00:09:30.516
lt's time for him to play His flute.

131
00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:31.784
What are you saying?
- Try to hear with devotion.

132
00:09:31.857 --> 00:09:35.293
Listen, you can hear
the echo of Mathura.

133
00:09:38.256 --> 00:09:41.521
Rajastan, Om Sai Ram.

134
00:09:43.989 --> 00:09:45.251
Heard it?

135
00:09:45.321 --> 00:09:46.982
Can you hear?
- Yes, yes.

136
00:09:47.288 --> 00:09:50.689
Now leave. - Sell this idol to me.
Please, Mr. Kanji.

137
00:09:50.754 --> 00:09:52.847
l'll let this idol out of my sight..

138
00:09:52.887 --> 00:09:54.718
..only when that
special person arrives.

139
00:09:54.786 --> 00:09:56.253
The chosen one.

140
00:09:56.286 --> 00:09:58.550
Who is that?

141
00:09:58.853 --> 00:10:01.413
The sage had said that
''A great devotee of Sai..

142
00:10:01.719 --> 00:10:05.917
''..from Rajasthan
will come for His ldol''.

143
00:10:06.452 --> 00:10:07.942
That's amazing.
- What?

144
00:10:08.252 --> 00:10:10.311
That's me.
- No, no.

145
00:10:10.384 --> 00:10:11.544
Look, there's my car.

146
00:10:11.651 --> 00:10:12.743
RJ, Rajasthan.

147
00:10:14.251 --> 00:10:16.378
And it also has an 'Om Sai' sticker.

148
00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:17.639
That's true.

149
00:10:17.717 --> 00:10:18.911
What did you say your name was?

150
00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.511
Bhanwar Lal.
- Bhanwar Lal?

151
00:10:22.649 --> 00:10:25.550
Mahadev...it's him?
- What?

152
00:10:26.249 --> 00:10:27.580
Who?
- lt's him?

153
00:10:28.315 --> 00:10:30.977
What happened? - The sage had
written your name himself.

154
00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:32.370
Look.

155
00:10:32.448 --> 00:10:33.847
Bhanwar Lal.

156
00:10:33.881 --> 00:10:36.907
l don't understand
a word that's written here.

157
00:10:36.981 --> 00:10:38.642
lt's written in Madrasi.

158
00:10:38.714 --> 00:10:41.547
He was a Madrasi.
Though he lived in Dwarka but, look..

159
00:10:42.247 --> 00:10:43.771
Great.

160
00:10:43.846 --> 00:10:45.370
This idol now belongs to you.

161
00:10:45.846 --> 00:10:47.245
Thank you.

162
00:10:47.312 --> 00:10:48.370
Great.

163
00:10:48.446 --> 00:10:50.311
Kanji Money?
- Bhanwar Lal.

164
00:10:50.378 --> 00:10:52.243
You only listen, but don't understand.

165
00:10:52.511 --> 00:10:54.672
l said l won't
charge you for this idol..

166
00:10:54.744 --> 00:10:57.269
..but l will have to pay the sage.

167
00:10:57.344 --> 00:10:58.606
Yes, of course.

168
00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:02.379
Here you go. 100 rupees.

169
00:11:03.177 --> 00:11:05.611
Only 100..
- Mahadev. Mahadev.

170
00:11:05.877 --> 00:11:08.607
This is a question of devotion.
We cannot force anyone.

171
00:11:09.442 --> 00:11:11.239
Do you how much l had at that time?

172
00:11:11.308 --> 00:11:12.605
Only 20 rupees.

173
00:11:12.675 --> 00:11:13.835
Only 20 rupees. Remember?

174
00:11:13.875 --> 00:11:14.864
So do you know what l did?

175
00:11:15.175 --> 00:11:19.168
l was wearing a similar gold chain.
And l gave that to him.

176
00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.171
lt's all about faith.

177
00:11:21.241 --> 00:11:22.606
Anything you give is less.

178
00:11:22.673 --> 00:11:23.901
Anything you give is less.

179
00:11:24.174 --> 00:11:25.732
Wow. What a thought.

180
00:11:25.807 --> 00:11:29.470
Not just my gold chain,
l will give up my gold ring too.

181
00:11:29.539 --> 00:11:31.302
That's it.

182
00:11:31.372 --> 00:11:32.805
Here. Here you go.
- Great. Take of everything.

183
00:11:32.873 --> 00:11:34.204
Take of everything.
- Take it.

184
00:11:34.572 --> 00:11:35.869
Great, great, great.

185
00:11:36.372 --> 00:11:40.308
Glory to..
- Lord Krishna!

186
00:11:41.371 --> 00:11:42.360
Glory.

187
00:11:42.438 --> 00:11:43.530
Now, where will this idol emerge from?

188
00:11:43.604 --> 00:11:45.868
From the land of Mathura, where else?

189
00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:50.499
Glory to Sri Kanji Lalji Mehta.

190
00:11:50.603 --> 00:11:52.628
Glory to you.

191
00:11:52.703 --> 00:11:54.830
As long as people
believe in toys like this..

192
00:11:54.869 --> 00:11:57.565
..our business will prosper.

193
00:11:57.635 --> 00:12:01.196
Kanji. This is the God's idol,
don't call it a toy.

194
00:12:01.268 --> 00:12:05.295
The Lord is only a delusion.
- Yes, let's go.

195
00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:12.427
lsn't that Chintu?

196
00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.199
Yes.

197
00:12:14.666 --> 00:12:16.395
Yes, that's him.
- Yes.

198
00:12:16.498 --> 00:12:20.093
Yes. He's dancing so well.

199
00:12:20.165 --> 00:12:22.224
l'll put an end to all this.

200
00:12:22.365 --> 00:12:24.629
Shut down the shop and
get the scooter. - Yes.

201
00:12:25.664 --> 00:12:28.132
Come on.
- Kanji. - Yes.

202
00:12:28.197 --> 00:12:29.755
Look after my shop for a month.

203
00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.297
Why?
- l'm going on Haj.

204
00:12:31.597 --> 00:12:33.189
l suggest that you
get your shop fixed..

205
00:12:33.263 --> 00:12:34.423
..rather than going on a Haj.

206
00:12:34.496 --> 00:12:35.656
God save me from devils.

207
00:12:35.729 --> 00:12:39.392
Your shop will come crashing
down even if anyone sneezes.

208
00:12:43.695 --> 00:12:45.253
Let's go.
- Coming.

209
00:12:47.394 --> 00:12:49.362
Feed them worth 10 rupees.
- Okay.

210
00:12:50.627 --> 00:12:51.651
Let's go, let's go.

211
00:12:54.227 --> 00:12:57.355
Glory to..
- Siddeshwar Maharaj.

212
00:12:57.392 --> 00:13:02.125
Let the 'Janmastami'
festivities begin.

